Original commit body from e318c3c6ce17daea97c1f1aad3cf578b45b72ec9:

ADR-0057 §5 rules that which producer wins a contested categorical
attribute is a preference with one built-in default, never a hardcoded
"type-aware wins". Until now the order was inferred in three places
(registry.incumbent_first, the merge pass, finalize 7a) and the two
declared levels were module constants. Now `hypergumbo_core.arbitration`
is the one place precedence is computed:

- ArbitrationPolicy(prefer, prefer_by_attribute, corroborated_confidence,
  superseded_stub_rank_factor); BUILTIN_POLICY = incumbent first (the
  registry's inference), 0.95, 0.5, no per-attribute exception.
- `[merge]` in either ADR-0045 preference tier: `prefer` orders BACKENDS
  (one line means the same thing for every language the backend serves),
  `[merge.prefer_by_attribute]` replaces it per attribute, the two levels
  move. Project tier replaces user tier key by key. Refused naming the
  file and key, BEFORE any analysis runs (exit 2): an unknown key, a
  backend no registered analyzer declares, an attribute the merge pass
  does not arbitrate, a level outside [0, 1] (bool is not 1).
- run_survey resolves the policy once and threads it into
  merge_producer_records (precedence, per-attribute precedence, the §13
  level) and FinalizeContext.arbitration_policy → demote_superseded_stubs
  (producer order, the §14 factor). The constants are re-exported from
  merge_producers / finalize under their old names.
- §10 citation gate: BUILTIN_ATTRIBUTE_EXCEPTIONS is EMPTY — the first
  backend-agreement table (docs/audits/0019) warranted none — and
  validate_builtin_exceptions refuses, by name, any future entry that does
  not cite a committed docs/audits/ document of kind backend_agreement
  (live-tree test).
- Which arm is the ALTERNATIVE stays a registry fact
  (ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS, now read through registry.incumbents_of by the
  recorded-producer-input lint); which arm WINS is the policy's.

Acceptance (the item's): a config.toml naming a per-attribute order changes
the arbitrated scalar on the contested attribute in the artifact and
nothing else (pipeline test on the second-Python-producer fixture: Alias
variable → type_alias, every other (name, kind, origin, span) identical);
an unknown key under [merge] exits 2 naming .hypergumbo.toml and the key.
On the recorded aardvark-dns fixture a kind preference for the SCIP arm
moves exactly the kind row's carried value (constant ← variable x15) and
no other count; the committed 0019 table is unchanged under the built-in.
Eight mutations each kill 1–5 tests. Not done, stated: no CLI flag or
environment variable spells a precedence (no measurement has asked for a
one-off override).

